From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:18:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/29] usb: gadget: f_acm: do not requeue RX requests on
 shutdown

When the endpoint is disabled the pending OUT request is given back with
-ESHUTDOWN. Queueing it again had it given back again, so stopping the
USB serial console never returned.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
index b6c11d97..b5667a8c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
@@ -293,6 +293,13 @@ static void acm_rx_complete(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *req)
 {
 	struct f_acm *f_acm = req->context;
 
+	/*
+	 * The endpoint is being disabled: queueing the request again would
+	 * have it given back again, forever.
+	 */
+	if (req->status == -ESHUTDOWN || req->status == -ECONNRESET)
+		return;
+
 	buf_push(&f_acm->rx_buf, req->buf, req->actual);
 
 	/* Queue RX req again */
